!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section O3: O3+hv->O2+O(3P)
! No change with respect to the previous versions (crs2004)
! Rem1: Quantum yield depends on temperature and is computed in subroutine CALC_QY_O3.
! Rem2: Temperature influence:
!    i) 116.3-277.8nm: T indep.
!   ii) 277.8-347.5nm: T dep. according to the formula (Molina & molina 1986,JGR,Vol.91,pp.14501-14508):
!           crs(T) = crs_on_file + tb_o3*(T-230) + tc_o3*(T-230)**2 ; T(K)
!       where tb_o3 and tc_o3 are parameters provided below in the last two columns.
!       crs_on_file are the values in the fourth column below.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!  iii) 347.5-735.0nm: T indep.
! Rem3: In ranges 116.3-362.5nm and 407.5-735 nm. Same crs,tb_o3 & tc_o3 for iproc=18.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :         1 | Finishes at wl interval :   171
